Docker 
A Docker image is a read-only blueprint that contains the application, dependencies, and configurations needed to create a container.

A Docker container is a running instance of an image. It is mutable (i.e., it can have a writable layer), and you can start, stop, or remove it.

CMD :
  -Provides a default command for the container.	
  -Overridable?	Yes, users can override it when running the container.
  -Syntax	CMD ["executable", "arg1", "arg2"]
ENTRYPOINT:
  -Defines the main executable of the container.
	-No, unless using the --entrypoint flag.
	-ENTRYPOINT ["executable", "arg1", "arg2"]

